---

<DocsLayout title="Terminal" description="Integrated terminal in Axon">
  <h1>Integrated Terminal</h1>

  <p>
    Axon includes a PTY-backed integrated terminal owned by the Go backend and
    rendered through xterm.js. You can run commands, use Git, start tools, and
    keep terminal sessions alive while the panel hides, the renderer reconnects,
    or the workbench changes state.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img src="/media/screenshots/axon-screenshot-09.png" alt="Axon integrated terminal and output panel inside the editor workspace" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>The terminal is treated as a first-class workspace surface with persistent sessions and editor-aware controls.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Opening the Terminal</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Click the Terminal icon in the sidebar</li>
    <li>Use keyboard shortcut: <code>Ctrl+`</code> (or <code>Cmd+`</code> on macOS)</li>
    <li>From the command palette: <code>Toggle Terminal</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Terminal Tabs</h2>
  <p>
    Create multiple terminal sessions and switch between them using tabs. Each
    tab runs its own shell process, and replay state is tracked so output can
    be restored when the renderer reconnects.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>New tab</strong> — Click the + button or use <code>Ctrl+Shift+`</code></li>
    <li><strong>Close tab</strong> — Click the X or use <code>Ctrl+Shift+W</code></li>
    <li><strong>Rename tab</strong> — Double-click the tab title</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Shell Configuration</h2>
  <p>
    Axon respects your default system shell. On macOS and Linux, it uses the
    shell specified in <code>$SHELL</code>. On Windows, it uses PowerShell by
    default (configurable in settings).
  </p>

  <h2>Terminal Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Full PTY support for interactive programs (vim, htop, etc.)</li>
    <li>Copy/paste with <code>Ctrl+Shift+C</code> / <code>Ctrl+Shift+V</code></li>
    <li>Select text with mouse or keyboard</li>
    <li>WebSocket connection to Go backend for real-time I/O</li>
    <li>Persistent sessions across window reloads</li>
    <li>Scrollback replay when a terminal view reconnects</li>
    <li>Backpressure handling for long-running agent output</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Axon CLI</h2>
  <p>
    The terminal also connects to the <code>axon</code> command. Use
    <code>axon</code> for an interactive Axon Agent session,
    <code>axon .</code> to open the current project in a new Axon window, and
    <code>axon resume</code> to continue a saved workspace conversation.
  </p>

  <h2>Customizing the Terminal</h2>
  <p>
    Terminal appearance can be customized in Settings:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{terminalThemeExample}</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
